PDB — PodDisruptionBudget
A PDB helps protect application availability during supported voluntary disruptions, such as node draining for maintenance.

For example, if you run five replicas and want at least four to remain available during maintenance, define a PDB with minAvailable: 4.

apiVersion: policy/v1
kind: PodDisruptionBudget
metadata:
  name: web-pdb
  namespace: prod
spec:
  minAvailable: 4
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: web-app

The selector must match the labels on your Deployment's Pods.


kubectl get pdb -n prod
kubectl describe pdb web-pdb -n prod
kubectl drain <node-name> --ignore-daemonsets
